  "title": "Watson Brake mounds",
  "summary": "Watson Brake, on the Ouachita River floodplain near Monroe in northern Louisiana, has at least 11 mounds of three to 25 feet tall linked by ridges into an oval 853 feet across. Dated to 5400 B.P., it is about 1,900 years older than Poverty Point. Researchers concluded mobile hunter-gatherers used it as a seasonal base from summer through fall.",
